==English==

===Pronunciation===
*{{RP}} {{IPA|/sʌbˈmæɹɪnə/}}
{{rfp|US pronunciation needed}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A member of the [[crew]] of a [[submarine]].
#{{context|US|baseball}} A [[pitcher]] that throws with an underhand motion.
#: ''Jones was a '''submariner''' and could often confuse a batter with his unorthodox delivery.''

====Usage notes====
*This word is sometimes pronounced like ''[[sub-]]'' + ''[[mariner]]''; however, since the prefix ''sub-'' can imply inferiority (as in ''[[subpar]]'' or ''[[subhuman]]''), this pronunciation can be considered offensive by some, especially in the US. The pronunciation ''[[submarine]]'' + ''[[-er]]'', but with stress on third syllable, is therefore preferred by many or most submarine crew members today.

